#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2316 expect=noViolation domain=TX
#note "SET01 carries a TXPARMCD=TCNTRL record, so the study declares a 'Control Type' somewhere in TX -> no violation. The rule is dataset-level ('No Trial Set with TCNTRL Parameter'), so SET02 not carrying TCNTRL is deliberately not flagged."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset TX class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Sets"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SETCD    type=Char label="Set Code"
col SET      type=Char label="Set Description"
col TXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TXPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Short Name"
col TXPARM   type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter"
col TXVAL    type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Value"
---
S01 | TX | SET01 | Control   | 1 | TCNTRL | Control Type | VEHICLE
S01 | TX | SET01 | Control   | 2 | GRPLBL | Group Label  | Control
S01 | TX | SET02 | High Dose | 3 | GRPLBL | Group Label  | High Dose
